  "notes": "Geometry from a right-side photo of XA-DAE (July 2025) mirrored; N110JS (Apr 2025) confirms the left side. The title is read as all-caps with larger initials; the red line's path is approximate. Re-checked 2026-11-15 on XA-DAE (flipped) fitted to the measured 737-800 shape (the fit puts the windows about 0.05 high in y, taken out): the red swoosh is one tapering line, not two: from a point about 1 m aft of the forward door (x 0.155) it runs just under the windows to x 0.29, rises across them to its top over the wing root (x 0.47 to 0.54, y 0.37) and fades aft at x 0.61; drawn as one smooth area. The title runs x 0.154 to 0.316, baseline about 0.26 m above the windows' middle, its big initials 0.86 m above it (height 0.26). The navy's front edge and its mid-blue edging are curves: smooth.",
  "history": "Replaces Skyarium v1's approximate standard (a few colors from memory). The 2017 livery accompanied Aeroméxico's rebrand (navy replacing the earlier lighter blue)."
